      "content": "That framework makes sense. I want to dig a bit deeper into the 'demographic volatility' and 'economic factors' sections. In certain metropolitan areas, we see specific neighborhoods that have very high concentrations of certain ethnic or immigrant populations that are also experiencing rapid shifts in socioeconomic status. \n\nIf we're trying to be as accurate as possible for the city council, should we include specific ethnic density or migration patterns as a sub-variable under volatility? I'm wondering if those specific demographic clusters are more predictive of sudden 'unrest' than general economic data alone.",
